 1/3 compuesto y Romberg con la referencia analítica.","tables":[{"title":"Distancia de frenado = ∫₀ᵀ v(t) dt (v lineal)","headers":["Subintervalos n","Trapecio (m)","Error trapecio","Simpson 1/3 (m)","Error Simpson"],"rows":[[2,"25","0","25","0"],[4,"25","0","25","0"],[8,"25","0","25","0"],[16,"25","0","25","0"],[32,"25","0","25","0"]],"note":"Referencia v₀²/(2a) = 25 m. El trapecio es exacto para integrandos lineales."},{"title":"Romberg sobre v(t)","headers":["Nivel","R(i,0)","R(i,1)","R(i,2)","R(i,3)","R(i,4)"],"rows":[[0,"25","","","",""],[1,"25","25","","",""],[2,"25","25","25","",""],[3,"25","25","25","25",""],[4,"25","25","25","25","25"]],"note":""},{"title":"Ampliación: ∫ v_c(t) dt (integrando exponencial) hasta t = 3.4657359 s","headers":["n","Trapecio","Error","Orden","Simpson","Error","Orden"],"rows":[[2,"15.84211383","0.49947286","—","15.34659193","0.00395096","—"],[4,"15.46769637","0.1250554","1.99783894","15.34289055","0.00024958","3.98463275"],[8,"15.37391655","0.03127558","1.99945879","15.34265661","1.564e-5","3.99613858"],[16,"15.3504606","0.00781963","1.99986464","15.34264195","9.782e-7","3.99903342"],[32,"15.34459593","0.00195495","1.99996616","15.34264103","6.115e-8","3.99975844"],[64,"15.34312971","0.00048874","1.99999154","15.34264098","3.822e-9","3.9999394"]],"note":"Referencia analítica 15.34264097 m. Romberg (7 niveles): 15.342640972003 (error 1.776e-15)."}],"plots":[{"title":"Ampliación: error de integración vs n (log-log)","xLabel":"Subintervalos n","yLabel":"Error absoluto (m)","logX":true,"logY":true,"series":[{"name":"Trapecio","points":[[2,0.4994728577],[4,0.1250553991],[8,0.03127558017],[16,0.007819628683],[32,0.001954953031],[64,0.0004887411241]],"markers":true},{"name":"Simpson 1/3","points":[[2,0.00395096295],[4,0.0002495795392],[8,0.00001564052759],[16,9.781881207e-7],[32,6.114699502e-8],[64,3.821847727e-9]],"markers":true}]}]},{"id":"errores","title":"Errores, sensibilidad y análisis estadístico","intro":"Teoría de errores transversal: errores por método, sensibilidad relativa (amplificación ≈ variación relativa del resultado / variación relativa del dato) y propagación estocástica con semilla fija (reproducible).","tables":[{"title":"Tabla de errores por método (Eₐ, Eᵣ, Eₚ)","headers":["Método / magnitud","Aproximación","Referencia","Eₐ","Eᵣ","Eₚ"],"rows":[["Bisección · t_det (s)","5","5","2.910e-11","5.821e-12","5.821e-10 %"],["Newton · t_det (s)","5","5","0","0","0 %"],["Secante · t_det (s)","5","5","0","0","0 %"],["RK2 · x(T) (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["RK4 · x(T) (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["Trapecio n=32 · d_fren (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["Simpson n=32 · d_fren (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["Romberg · d_fren (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"]],"note":""},{"title":"Sensibilidad de d_total y t_det ante +1 % en un parámetro","headers":["Parámetro","Δ d_total (m)","Δ d_total (%)","Amplificación d_total","Amplificación t_det"],"rows":[["v₀","0.6525","1.63125 %","1.63125","1"],["a","-0.24752475","-0.61881188 %","-0.61881188","-0.99009901"],["tᵣ","0.15","0.375 %","0.375","0"]],"note":"Amplificación = (Δy/y)/(Δp/p). La distancia total suma un término lineal en v₀ (reacción) y uno cuadrático (frenado, ∝ v₀²), por eso la amplificación respecto de v₀ queda entre 1 y 2."},{"title":"Monte Carlo (N = 2000, semilla 20261112): distribución de d_total","headers":["Estadístico","Valor (m)"],"rows":[["Media","40.49201035"],["Desv. estándar","5.5784173"],["Percentil 5","31.62456727"],["Mediana","40.57591905"],["Percentil 95","49.604359"],["Máximo","55.52845992"],["P(d_total > 60 m)","0 %"]],"note":"Incertidumbres sintéticas: v₀ ±5 %, a ±20 %, tᵣ ±50 % (distribuciones uniformes). Ilustra propagación, no mide un riesgo real."}],"plots":[{"title":"Distribución Monte Carlo de la distancia total","xLabel":"Distancia total (m)","yLabel":"Frecuencia relativa","kind":"bars","series":[{"name":"Frecuencia","points":[[27.4566356,0.0045],[28.65118131,0.008],[29.84572703,0.0145],[31.04027275,0.024],[32.23481846,0.041],[33.42936418,0.044],[34.62390989,0.0525],[35.81845561,0.0755],[37.01300133,0.064],[38.20754704,0.069],[39.40209276,0.0705],[40.59663847,0.0825],[41.79118419,0.074],[42.9857299,0.072],[44.18027562,0.065],[45.37482134,0.061],[46.56936705,0.0535],[47.76391277,0.037],[48.95845848,0.035],[50.1530042,0.021],[51.34754992,0.0125],[52.54209563,0.0095],[53.73664135,0.0055],[54.93118706,0.004]]}],"vlines":[{"x":60,"label":"Distancia disponible"},{"x":40,"label":"Determinista"}]}]}],"metric":{"label":"Distancia total","value":40,"unit":"m"},"numeric":"Con a constante, RK2 y RK4 reproducen x(t) salvo redondeo (error máx. 0 m). Newton y secante hallan T = v₀/a en 1 y 2 iteraciones (función lineal), la bisección requiere 35. En la ampliación v′ = −(a + c·v) los órdenes observados son ≈ 2.054 (RK2) y ≈ 4.06 (RK4). Trapecio y Simpson integran v(t) lineal sin error; el orden real aparece con el integrando exponencial.","physical":"Con los parámetros sintéticos la cabina necesita 5 s y 25 m para detenerse tras frenar, más 15 m durante la reacción (total 40 m). Queda un margen de 20 m respecto de la distancia disponible declarada; la propagación Monte Carlo estima P(d_total > 60 m) ≈ 0 %. La distancia crece con v₀² y con tᵣ; la desaceleración influye como 1/a. No se infieren distancias ni protocolos reales de seguridad.","note":"Parámetros sintéticos y supuestos; sin relación con equipos reales de Mi Teleférico.","caseId":1,"scenario":"NORMAL","params":{"v0":10,"a":2,"tr":1.5,"h":1,"c":0.2,"dAvail":60},"model":"v(t) = v₀ − at;  x(t) = v₀t − ½at²;  t_det = v₀/a;  d_fren = v₀²/(2a)","engine":"semana3-v1.0","runMeta":[{"family":"Raíces","method":"Bisección","nIter":35},{"family":"Raíces","method":"Newton-Raphson","nIter":2},{"family":"Raíces","method":"Secante","nIter":3},{"family":"EDO","method":"RK2 (punto medio)","nIter":6},{"family":"EDO","method":"RK4","nIter":6},{"family":"EDO","method":"RK4 · ampliación v′ = −(a + c·v)","nIter":5},{"family":"Integración","method":"Trapecio compuesto","nIter":5},{"family":"Integración","method":"Simpson 1/3 compuesto","nIter":5},{"family":"Integración","method":"Romberg","nIter":5}]}');
