,"0 %"],["RK2 · x(T) (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["RK4 · x(T) (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["Trapecio n=32 · d_fren (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["Simpson n=32 · d_fren (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"],["Romberg · d_fren (m)","25","25","0","0","0 %"]],"note":""},{"title":"Sensibilidad de d_total y t_det ante +1 % en un parámetro","headers":["Parámetro","Δ d_total (m)","Δ d_total (%)","Amplificación d_total","Amplificación t_det"],"rows":[["v₀","0.6525","1.63125 %","1.63125","1"],["a","-0.24752475","-0.61881188 %","-0.61881188","-0.99009901"],["tᵣ","0.15","0.375 %","0.375","0"]],"note":"Amplificación = (Δy/y)/(Δp/p). La distancia total suma un término lineal en v₀ (reacción) y uno cuadrático (frenado, ∝ v₀²), por eso la amplificación respecto de v₀ queda entre 1 y 2."},{"title":"Monte Carlo (N = 2000, semilla 20261112): distribución de d_total","headers":["Estadístico","Valor (m)"],"rows":[["Media","40.49201035"],["Desv. estándar","5.5784173"],["Percentil 5","31.62456727"],["Mediana","40.57591905"],["Percentil 95","49.604359"],["Máximo","55.52845992"],["P(d_total > 60 m)","0 %"]],"note":"Incertidumbres sintéticas: v₀ ±5 %, a ±20 %, tᵣ ±50 % (distribuciones uniformes). Ilustra propagación, no mide un riesgo real."}],"plots":[{"title":"Distribución Monte Carlo de la distancia total","xLabel":"Distancia total (m)","yLabel":"Frecuencia relativa","kind":"bars","series":[{"name":"Frecuencia","points":[[27.4566356,0.0045],[28.65118131,0.008],[29.84572703,0.0145],[31.04027275,0.024],[32.23481846,0.041],[33.42936418,0.044],[34.62390989,0.0525],[35.81845561,0.0755],[37.01300133,0.064],[38.20754704,0.069],[39.40209276,0.0705],[40.59663847,0.0825],[41.79118419,0.074],[42.9857299,0.072],[44.18027562,0.065],[45.37482134,0.061],[46.56936705,0.0535],[47.76391277,0.037],[48.95845848,0.035],[50.1530042,0.021],[51.34754992,0.0125],[52.54209563,0.0095],[53.73664135,0.0055],[54.93118706,0.004]]}],"vlines":[{"x":60,"label":"Distancia disponible"},{"x":40,"label":"Determinista"}]}]}],"metric":{"label":"Distancia total","value":40,"unit":"m"},"numeric":"La raíz triple de v₀(1−t/T)³ hace que Newton y la secante pasen de convergencia superlineal/cuadrática a lineal (razón ≈ 0.66666667); el error en t tras 25 iteraciones de Newton es 0.00015841 s aunque el residual sea 3.180e-13. El Newton modificado (m = 3) recupera convergencia en 1 paso(s). Bisección no depende de la derivada pero converge solo linealmente (÷2 por paso). Esto es mal condicionamiento de la raíz, no falta de convergencia ni peligro físico.","physical":"Con los parámetros sintéticos la cabina necesita 5 s y 25 m para detenerse tras frenar, más 15 m durante la reacción (total 40 m). Queda un margen de 20 m respecto de la distancia disponible declarada; la propagación Monte Carlo estima P(d_total > 60 m) ≈ 0 %. La distancia crece con v₀² y con tᵣ; la desaceleración influye como 1/a. No se infieren distancias ni protocolos reales de seguridad.","note":"MAL CONDICIONADO es aquí un subexperimento de raíces (multiplicidad 3); las tablas de EDO e integración usan el modelo lineal base.","caseId":1,"scenario":"MAL CONDICIONADO","params":{"v0":10,"a":2,"tr":1.5,"h":1,"c":0.2,"dAvail":60},"model":"v(t) = v₀ − at;  x(t) = v₀t − ½at²;  t_det = v₀/a;  d_fren = v₀²/(2a)","engine":"semana3-v1.0","runMeta":[{"family":"Raíces","method":"Bisección","nIter":11},{"family":"Raíces","method":"Newton-Raphson","nIter":26},{"family":"Raíces","method":"Secante","nIter":35},{"family":"Raíces","method":"Newton modificado (m=3)","nIter":2},{"family":"EDO","method":"RK2 (punto medio)","nIter":6},{"family":"EDO","method":"RK4","nIter":6},{"family":"EDO","method":"RK4 · ampliación v′ = −(a + c·v)","nIter":5},{"family":"Integración","method":"Trapecio compuesto","nIter":5},{"family":"Integración","method":"Simpson 1/3 compuesto","nIter":5},{"family":"Integración","method":"Romberg","nIter":5}]}');
